rtl8812au: build against Linux 6.12

Build fixes for aircrack-ng/rtl8812au at commit ee6490b ("Turn of
CONFIG_MP_INCLUDED"), which is what `make` needs before the driver will even
compile on a current kernel. Measured on Debian 13, kernel 6.12.113.

Four changes, all of them API drift rather than behaviour:

  1. cfg80211_rtw_change_beacon() takes struct cfg80211_ap_update * instead of
     struct cfg80211_beacon_data * (kernel 6.12).
  2. cfg80211_rtw_set_monitor_channel() gained a struct net_device * argument
     (kernel 6.12).
  3. strlcpy() is gone from the kernel headers; strscpy() has the same call
     shape for these uses.
  4. .usbdrv.drvwrap.driver.shutdown no longer exists (kernel 6.5); the driver's
     shutdown hook is not settable that way any more.
  5. REGULATORY_IGNORE_STALE_KICKOFF is not exported by every kernel's headers
     (Debian 6.12 does not have it). It is only a hint, so it is skipped.

Apply with scripts/build_rtl8812au.sh, which detects a fresh tree, an already
patched tree and a base mismatch separately.

Note that all of this is *compilation*. The behaviour this project depends on -
AP mode plus nl80211 .mgmt_tx on the AP interface - is driver-independent, and
was verified separately; see docs/HARDWARE_CHECKLIST.md stage 4.

